---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import VlanDesigner from '../../components/VlanDesigner';
---
<Base title="VLAN Designer" description="Design VLANs visually: assign ports, set who may talk to whom, test a ping, and export RouterOS scripts for the switch and router.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">VLAN designer</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-muted">
      Design a small VLAN network end to end. Assign switch ports, decide which VLANs may reach each other, then send
      test pings and watch exactly where they succeed or get dropped. When you are happy, export scripts for the switch
      and the router.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8"><VlanDesigner client:load /></div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-muted">
      New to VLANs? Read <a class="text-accent underline" href="/learn/foundations/04-switching-and-vlans">Switching &amp; VLANs</a>{' '}
      and <a class="text-accent underline" href="/learn/mikrotik/02-bridge-and-vlans">Bridge and VLAN filtering</a>, then build it in the{' '}
      <a class="text-accent underline" href="/labs/inter-vlan-routing">inter-VLAN routing lab</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
